{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3400","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3400","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3400\",\"parent_revision\":\"16bb6e3dac5d73009ec3c631c1259a1bf585fc65ad8c56fa8374d954c4114ef7\",\"root_revision\":\"16bb6e3dac5d73009ec3c631c1259a1bf585fc65ad8c56fa8374d954c4114ef7\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-09-04\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/interop/SKILL.md` Step 3 (lines 87-95) has a mermaid flow that calls `backlog_add` and branches `CheckError{Response has error key?}` \u2192 `Yes: ABORT` (prints the error, does not capture the new issue number, does not write `**Backlog item:** #N` into the plan file).\\n\\nAfter #3182's fix, `backlog_add`/`add_item` can return a populated `error` on a call where the item WAS still stored locally \u2014 the \\\"GitHub issue creation attempted and failed\\\" branch (`item_ref`/local storage succeeds, `result[\\\"error\\\"]` carries the reason). Read literally, this flow's ABORT branch would discard that successfully-stored item and never write its reference into the plan file \u2014 the same contradiction `create/start.md` had before #3182's T5 task fixed it there.\\n\\nNot in #3182's original Impact Radius (interop/SKILL.md was not found as a consumer of `backlog_add`'s response contract during grooming); discovered by dh:service-docs-maintainer while implementing T5's equivalent fix in a sibling doc.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the fix pattern is already established in `create/start.md` Step 5 (post-#3182) \u2014 branch on a populated `error` separately from \\\"no item created,\\\" report the error, but still capture the issue number/reference and proceed rather than aborting. The same treatment likely applies here, but the exact wording is design work for grooming, not prescribed here.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality vigilance concern from #3182\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-04\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d84adea2c3e7cf8186f8e8aba2c237d02c5edfd2d335f004c3c5b236d0af012d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABStokcw\"}"}